---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Blog" sideBarActiveItemID="blog">
  <article class="mt-5 max-w-2xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight">Why I stopped writing tech blogs</h1>

    <div class="mt-8 text-lg leading-relaxed opacity-80 grid gap-5">
      <p>
        In the era of LLMs, I don't think writing tech blogs is as necessary as it once was.
      </p>
      <p>
        There was a time when I'd spend my evenings turning something I had just figured out into a post, hoping it
        would save someone else a few hours of frustration. Today, anyone can ask an LLM and get a clear, patient
        explanation in seconds, shaped around exactly where they are stuck.
      </p>
      <p>
        So I stopped writing tutorials. When I write now, I write what I feel: the thoughts that don't fit into a
        prompt.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're here to learn something technical, LLMs are good enough. Honestly, they're a wonderful teacher.
      </p>
      <p>
        My earlier writing, and some of my more abstract thoughts, are kept as an archive.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">RIP Abstract Thoughts 🤔</h2>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://imamhossainroni.hashnode.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Read the archive on Hashnode ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
